      "name": "DisconnectFromBnet",
      "signature": "void DisconnectFromBnet(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Disconnects from Battle.net game server and cleans up Bnet client state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_pBnclientInterface is initialized (non-NULL)\n2. If initialized, reset connection attempt counter to 0\n3. Clear two state bytes at offsets 0x359 and 0x379 in g_pBnetGameData\n4. Output debug message \"Disconnect from BNET\n\"\n5. Call Ordinal_10001 (likely Storm_GetTickCount or equivalent)\n6. Call virtual function at g_pBnclientInterface[0x10] (likely Disconnect method)\n7. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf g_pBnclientInterface is NULL (not initialized), function returns immediately without any cleanup.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x359 - State byte offset in g_pBnetGameData (purpose: likely session flag)\n0x379 - State byte offset in g_pBnetGameData (purpose: likely connection status flag)\n0x10 - Offset in g_pBnclientInterface VTable for disconnect method\n\nStructure Layout:\ng_pBnclientInterface VTable:\n  Offset 0x10: Function pointer to disconnect method\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error handling. Function proceeds silently if g_pBnclientInterface is NULL.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
