      "name": "ProcessBnetClientMessages",
      "signature": "void ProcessBnetClientMessages(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Handles unit slot selection and text display in the unit slot UI.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify g_pUnitSlotDE (text display control) is initialized\n2. Call indirect method to retrieve current selection context\n3. Read slot index from ESP (pushed by context method)\n4. Dispatch to appropriate slot handler (0-6) via jump table:\n   - Slots 0-6 map to unit IDs 0x1433-0x1439 respectively\n   - Invalid indices map to 0xFFFFFFFF (no selection)\n5. Clear text display control\n6. If valid ID selected (>= 0):\n   - Call ValidateStringId to get unit name string\n   - Call TextBoxAddText to display in text control\n7. Call GetTickCount to update timing reference\n8. Calculate line spacing based on time delta:\n   - Subtract g_dwBaseTime from current time\n   - Multiply by 0x10624dd3 (magic constant for time scaling)\n   - Divide by 0x14 (20 decimal) for line count\n   - Increment result\n9. Call FUN_6fa8547c to format text with calculated line spacing\n10. Clear text display control (g_pUnitSlotDF)\n11. Convert formatted text to Unicode and add to display\n\nParameters:\nNone (operates on global state)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_pUnitSlotDE is NULL, function returns immediately\n- Invalid slot indices (>6) set g_dwSelectedUnitId to -1\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1433-0x1439: Unit IDs for slots 0-6\n- 0x10624dd3: Time scaling multiplier for line spacing calculation\n- 0x14: Divisor (20 decimal) for line spacing computation\n\nGlobal Variables:\n- g_pUnitSlotDE: Primary text display control\n- g_pUnitSlotDF: Secondary text display control\n- g_dwSelectedUnitId: Currently selected unit ID\n- g_pBnclientInterface: Client interface pointer\n- g_dwBaseTime: Time reference for calculations\n- DAT_6fa8f1dc: Format string reference\n- DAT_6fa8f1e4: Additional format reference\n\nError Handling:\nNone - function does not return error codes\nTime calculations may overflow if delta is very large\n\nStructure Layout:\nText display interface (via g_pBnclientInterface + 0x8c):\n- Offset 0x8c: Method to retrieve current selection context",
