      "name": "UpdateExpansionUnitDisplay",
      "signature": "void UpdateExpansionUnitDisplay(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Updates the UI display for all units in the expansion character list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if Expansion MPQ files are available using CheckExpansionMpqExists()\n2. Clear all text data lists for expansion UI elements\n3. If not in game or not connected to battle.net, iterate through unit list:\n   - Skip units outside melee count and expansion unit range\n   - For valid expansion units, set unit field values based on game state:\n     * If unit state=1: Display title tier information\n     * If unit state=0: Calculate and display full character title with decorations\n     * If unit state=2: Display simple expansion class name\n   - Build character title string combining class name, title tier, and decorations\n   - Add text to appropriate expansion UI textbox using StringAsciiToUnicode() conversion\n   - Increment expansion offset by 0x5d bytes for next unit\n\nParameters:\nNone. Uses global unit list (g_pUnitListHead) and expansion feature UI (g_pExpansionFeatureUI).\n\nReturns:\nNone. Updates global UI state in-place.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles character classes 0-6 with specific localized string IDs (0xfab-0xfad)\n- Applies bit mask operations for unit field flags based on unit flag bits\n- For character decorations (emblems), checks valid emblem icon indexes before display\n- Converts ASCII character names to Unicode for UI display\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xd: Expansion offset subtraction constant\n- 0x5d: Byte increment for next expansion unit display\n- 0x1419, 0x1416, 0x1417, 0x1418: String IDs for expansion status messages\n- 0x2a70, 0x58cb: String IDs for class and emblem text\n- 0xfab-0xfad, 0x1507: String IDs for character class names by index\n- 0xfd9: String ID for title tier/decoration prefix\n\nError Handling:\n- Asserts if unit state is invalid (not 0, 1, or 2) via FogAssert()\n- Calls FatalErrorExit() on assertion failure with error code 0xffffffff\n- Gracefully handles null title tier returns (skips title text if unavailable)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:c4f760f77449695a501453534a79da3f",
