      "name": "ReleaseAllUnits",
      "signature": "void ReleaseAllUnits(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Releases all units from the unit list and current unit data, clearing game state.\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Iterate through linked list starting at g_pUnitListHead\n  2. For each unit, release its composite data (offset 0x1b8) using ReleaseCompositeUnit\n  3. Release unit pool allocation\n  4. Follow next pointer (offset 0x1c8) until list ends\n  5. Clear g_pUnitListHead, g_dwPlayerCount, g_dwMeleeUnitCount, g_dwStateChangeFlag\n  6. If g_pCurrentUnitData exists and ref count (offset 0x1b4) is 0, release it\n  7. Clear g_pCurrentUnitData\n\n  Parameters:\n  (none)\n\n  Returns:\n  void - No return value\n\n  Special Cases:\n  - Empty unit list: Skips iteration, clears globals\n  - Current unit with active references: Skips ReleaseCompositeUnit, only calls ReleasePoolAllocation\n  - NULL pointers: Checked before dereferencing\n\n  Unit Structure Fields (offsets):\n  0x1b4 | 4 | Reference count | int | Indicates if unit has active references\n  0x1b8 | 4 | Composite data | void* | Pointer to composite unit data\n  0x1c8 | 4 | Next unit | int | Next unit in linked list",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:9388c10cb6694c3d101542e2791f3e48",
