      "name": "UpdateGameUIState",
      "signature": "dword UpdateGameUIState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Updates game UI state based on player expansion status and game conditions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if expansion MPQ file exists via CheckExpansionMpqExists()\n2. If expansion exists: Traverse player unit list to find the selected player and update expansion UI flags\n3. If expansion missing: Calculate player count conditions and set appropriate UI flags\n4. Allocate and initialize current unit data (0x1d0 bytes)\n5. Create composite unit with appropriate class/mode based on unit flags\n6. Apply emblem icon if unit has saved emblem data\n7. Set unit composite mode, scaled value, and field values\n8. Build inventory bit masks based on unit flags (expansion, mercenary, etc.)\n9. Initialize Unicode buffers and populate server/local message lists with player info\n10. Generate class-specific string ID and append unit name to message\n11. Add custom emblem string if present, otherwise add default message\n\nParameters: None (__stdcall, no parameters)\nReturns: 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles units with class ID 1 or 2 (special expansions) with specific message IDs (0x1419, 0x2a70)\n- Handles units with expansion features and mercenary flags specially\n- Creates fallback dummy unit (class 7) if composite unit creation fails\n- Validates string IDs before using them\n\nKey Globals:\n- g_pUnitListHead: Linked list of units\n- g_dwPlayerSelectCount: Current player selection index\n- g_pCurrentUnitData: Pointer to current unit structure (0x1d0 bytes)\n- g_dwUIStateFlags, g_pHasExpansionUI, g_pPlayerCountUI: UI state flags\n- g_pServerMessageList, g_pLocalMessageList: Message text buffers\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1d0: Size of unit data structure\n- 0x1c8: Offset to next unit pointer in unit list (offset 0x72 * 4)\n- 0x1a0-0x1b0: Class and flag offsets within unit structure\n- 0x80000001: Bitmask for negative number detection\n- String IDs: 0xfab-0xfad (class names), 0x1419/0x2a70 (expansion messages)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
