      "name": "CreateAndRegisterCompositeUnit",
      "signature": "int CreateAndRegisterCompositeUnit(Unicode * lpszUnitName, Unicode * lpszUnitClass, int nUnitId, char nUnitType)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Creates and registers a new composite game unit (player character) with equipment components.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x1D0 bytes for unit structure from heap\n2. Convert unit name parameter from Unicode to UTF-8, store at offset 0x00\n3. Copy unit class parameter as Unicode string at offset 0x80\n4. Zero-initialize component array at offset 0x180 (0x10 bytes)\n5. Zero-initialize component index array at offset 0x190 (0x10 bytes)\n6. Initialize flags and metadata fields (offsets 0x1A0-0x1CB)\n7. Fill component indices array with 0xFF sentinel values in loop\n8. Set unit type byte at offset 0x1A0 from param_4\n9. Set initialized flag at offset 0x181 to 0x01\n10. Create composite unit with CreateCompositeUnit passing components/indices\n11. Store composite unit pointer at offset 0x1B8 and unit ID at offset 0x1B4\n12. Initialize unit data fields and set composite mode to 5\n13. Link unit into global doubly-linked list (g_pUnitListHead)\n14. Increment global player count (g_dwPlayerCount)\n15. Update display with UpdateExpansionUnitDisplay\n16. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nlpszUnitName - Unicode string pointer for unit name/identifier (ECX register)\nlpszUnitClass - Unicode string pointer for unit class/type (EDX register)\ndwUnitId - Unit ID or configuration value (Stack[0x4])\nnUnitType - Unit type byte, stored at offset 0x1A0 (Stack[0x8])\n\nReturns:\nEAX = 1 (success, always returns 1)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:d2b7f4d68f2f4e62b6266863b2b9e5b2",
