      "name": "HandleBnetConnectionStateChange",
      "signature": "uint HandleBnetConnectionStateChange(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Handles Bnet connection state change events and manages message loop shutdown.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10003 (unknown Storm function) for initial processing\n2. Call Ordinal_10002 to check login completion status\n3. If login completed and g_dwBnetLoginState is 0, return success\n4. Otherwise, call Ordinal_10032(0) to perform cleanup\n5. Stop the main message loop via StopMessageLoop()\n6. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Always returns 1 (success/true)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If both Ordinal_10002 returns non-zero AND g_dwBnetLoginState == 0, early exit\n  - Otherwise proceeds to StopMessageLoop() regardless of prior conditions\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0 = Check for g_dwBnetLoginState == 0 condition\n  1 = Return value (success)\n\nError Handling:\n  No error handling; always succeeds and stops message loop\n\nOrdinals (Storm.dll):\n  Ordinal_10003 = Unknown Storm function (event processing)\n  Ordinal_10002 = Bnet login status check\n  Ordinal_10032(0) = Cleanup/deactivation routine",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
