      "name": "InitializePaletteFromPath",
      "signature": "dword InitializePaletteFromPath(char * szPalettePath, dword dwUnknown)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Initializes the game palette from file path, with string comparison validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set global flag DAT_6fa97c84 to 1 to indicate palette initialization in progress\n2. Format szPalettePath and dwUnknown into szLocalPath1 using wsprintfA template\n3. Format dwUnknown into szLocalPath2 using same template\n4. Load global palette pointer from PTR_s_palette_fechar_pal_dat_6fa8d440\n5. Compare szPalettePath and palette pointer byte-by-byte:\n   - Loop through both strings comparing each byte pair\n   - If bytes differ: palette mismatch detected, iVar2 set to -1\n   - If first byte is zero: strings equal, iVar2 set to 0\n   - Compare second byte if first bytes match\n   - Advance pointers by 2 bytes per iteration\n6. Set global DAT_6fa9790c = 1 if comparison succeeded (iVar2 == 0), else 0\n7. Call InitActPalette with formatted string parameters\n8. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  szPalettePath (ECX): Pointer to palette file path string to validate\n  dwUnknown (EDX): Parameter formatted into both string buffers\n\nReturns:\n  dword: Always returns 1 (success indicator)\n\nCalled by:\n  FUN_6fa85070, FUN_6fa78730, FUN_6fa79290, FUN_6fa81800, FUN_6fa7e4f0,\n  FUN_6fa7ccd0, FUN_6fa79ef0, InitializeGameplayScreen, FUN_6fa7cfc0,\n  InitializeGameState\n\nDependencies:\n  InitActPalette: Initializes palette with formatted paths\n  wsprintfA: Formats strings into buffers (called twice)\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  DAT_6fa97c84: Set to 1 at function start (initialization flag)\n  DAT_6fa9790c: Set to 1 if palette match, 0 if mismatch (comparison result)\n  PTR_s_palette_fechar_pal_dat_6fa8d440: Global palette pointer referenced for comparison\n\nSpecial Notes:\n  - The string comparison is case-sensitive and character-by-character\n  - Two 260-byte buffers allocated on stack (0x208 bytes total)\n  - Both format strings use same template: likely path construction\n  - Comparison logic uses conditional subtraction (SBB) for three-way result",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:5fa7ad124dff598da0a64a7f8c3a5de4",
