      "name": "ShowTitleMessageDialog",
      "signature": "void ShowTitleMessageDialog(Unicode * pMessageText, void * pDisconnectHandler)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "ShowTitleMessageDialog - Displays a title message dialog with formatted text and disconnect handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dispatch all queued pending control handlers from the handler queue\n2. Reset the pending handler count to 0\n3. Create title window background frame via CreateObjectByTypeFactory\n4. Queue the window to pending handlers and set unit flags\n5. Create title header element via CreateObjectByTypeFactory  \n6. Queue the header to pending handlers and set unit flags\n7. Create text box UI control for main message via CreateObjectByTypeFactory\n8. Parse main message text (from pMessageText) by splitting on newline characters\n9. Add each parsed line to the text box via TextBoxAddText\n10. Create button UI control via CreateObjectByTypeFactory\n11. Queue button to pending handlers and set unit flags\n12. Create second text box for subtitle via CreateObjectByTypeFactory\n13. Parse subtitle text (from register input) by splitting on newlines\n14. Add each parsed subtitle line to subtitle text box\n15. Store disconnect handler callback (pDisconnectHandler) to _g_pBnetDisconnectHandler\n\nParameters:\nECX (pMessageText): Unicode* - Primary message text with embedded \n line breaks\nEDX (pDisconnectHandler): void* - Callback handler function pointer (implicit parameter)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Supports multi-line messages separated by \n (newline) characters\n- Enforces max 64 (0x40) queued pending handlers - exits fatally if exceeded\n- Empty message text handled (creates text box with no lines)\n- Uses local 2048-byte (0x400 wchar_t) Unicode buffer for string parsing\n- All UI objects created via object factory pattern using type descriptors\n\nError Handling:\n- FogAssert + FatalErrorExit called if handler queue exceeds limit\n- No error recovery; fatal abort chosen for invalid states\n- Caller responsible for dialog state management and cleanup",
