      "comment": "Reinitialize login UI after CD key authentication error, handling BNet reconnection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set global BNet connection active flag\n2. Query current BNet connection state via vftable call (offset 0x74)\n3. If connected: get login status, disconnect if needed, finalize disconnect\n4. Attempt new BNet connection via ConnectToBattleNet()\n5. Clear pending control handler references (indices 0x4e, 0x44, 0x4d)\n6. Initialize UI screen via FUN_6fa85070()\n7. Verify UI object count < 64 (0x40) with FogAssert guards\n8. Create 10 UI objects via CreateObjectByTypeFactory factory pattern:\n   - DAT_6fa8faa0, DAT_6fa8fad0, DAT_6fa8fb90 (title/header controls)\n   - DAT_6fa8fbc0, DAT_6fa8fc80, DAT_6fa8fcb0 (text/message controls)\n   - DAT_6fa8fd10, DAT_6fa8fd40 (account/password input fields)\n   - DAT_6fa8fd70, DAT_6fa8fda0 (buttons)\n9. Store account input field pointer at g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x4e]\n10. Store password input field pointer at g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x44]\n11. Set input field constraints: account=0x10 (16 chars), password=0xd (13 chars)\n12. Configure input callbacks via SetEditDataField9B() and SetEditFieldValue()\n13. Load saved account name from registry (Diablo II\\Last BNet key)\n14. Link input fields for Tab navigation (bidirectional)\n15. Set initial input focus to account field\n16. Create dialog controls (buttons, scrollbars, etc.)\n17. Check music enabled flag and initialize music track\n18. Return to caller with UI initialized\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- ConnectToBattleNet() failure: returns immediately without UI initialization\n- Expansion check: conditionally creates additional UI elements (DAT_6fa8fc80)\n- Registry read: handles missing account name gracefully (uses empty string)\n- UI object overflow: FogAssert and FatalErrorExit if count exceeds 64\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x40 (64): Maximum UI object count before fatal error\n- 0x4e, 0x44, 0x4d: Control handler array indices for account/password/reserved\n- 0x1468, 0x1469, 0x1454, 0x1455: String table IDs for UI text\n- 0x10, 0xd: Max character lengths (16 for account, 13 for password)\n\nError Handling:\n- FogAssert guards prevent UI overflow (calls FatalErrorExit on violation)\n- Early exit if BNet connection fails\n- Graceful handling of missing registry values\n\nMemory Model:\n- Stack buffer [ESP + 0xc] sized 0x400 (1024 bytes) for registry string\n- All UI objects managed via global g_pUIObjectArray\n- Global counter g_dwUIObjectCount tracks creation\n- Handler pointers stored in g_aPendingControlHandlers array\n\nCalled by: FUN_6fa839f0 (error handler dispatcher)\nCalls: ConnectToBattleNet, DisconnectFromBnet, FinalizeBnetDisconnect, CreateObjectByTypeFactory, SetEditControlValue, SetEditDataField9B, SetEditFieldValue, LinkDoubleLinkedListNodes, ValidateStringId, TextBoxAddTextWithDefaults, TextBoxAddText, GetRegistryStringValue, ConvertCharToUnicodeAndSetEditData, FUN_6fa85070, FUN_6fa7a8a0, GetMusicOptions, InitializeMusicTrackState",
