      "name": "UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange",
      "signature": "void UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes the character selection screen UI and data structures.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fa84050() for screen initialization setup\n2. Dispatch all pending inventory item handlers via loop through g_pUIObjectArray\n3. Clear global UI object counters and state variables (_g_dw_Unknown1/2, g_dwUIObjectCount)\n4. Dispatch any remaining pending control handlers for prior screen\n5. Set global configuration and reinitialize palettes based on g_bPaletteReinitFlag\n6. Release all existing units and clear hash tables for clean slate\n7. Compare two palette file paths byte-by-byte (DAT_6fa8d440 vs DAT_6fa8d444)\n8. Initialize act palettes using the compared paths via InitActPalette\n9. Check MAX_CHILDREN assertion enforces limit of 0x40 UI objects per screen\n10. Create and register base UI objects in sequence: primary inventory, skill boxes, text containers\n11. Conditionally create expansion-specific UI objects if g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x59] == 1\n12. Check expansion status via CheckExpansionMpqExists to determine UI variant\n13. If no expansion, use classic UI objects; if expansion, use enhanced UI objects\n14. Create final configuration UI objects regardless of expansion (buttons, controls)\n15. Check g_dwBnetConnectionAttempts to conditionally initialize network-related UI\n16. Clear all object state bits via SetOrClearBitMask calls for each created object\n17. Call FUN_6fa7a7c0() for final screen setup and initialization completion\n18. Return to caller with all UI objects ready for interaction\n\nParameters:\nNone. Called as initialization routine from character select login flow.\n\nReturns:\nvoid. Function modifies global UI state: g_pUIObjectArray, g_dwUIObjectCount, and manages \nvarious DAT_* global references for created UI objects.",
