      "name": "GetGameState",
      "signature": "uint GetGameState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "unknown",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Retrieves the current game state value from global game state variable.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load DWORD from global game state address (0x6fa978bc)\n2. Return value in EAX\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: Current game state value (32-bit unsigned integer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This is a simple accessor function (leaf function, single instruction)\n- The global variable appears to be used across multiple UI initialization routines\n- Used during character select screen setup to configure edit field behavior\n\nStructure Layout - Global Game State:\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type     Description\n  ------  ----  -----         ----     -----------\n  0x00    4     dwGameState   uint     Current game state flags/value\n",
