      "name": "HandlePendingCharacterSelection",
      "signature": "dword HandlePendingCharacterSelection(int nControlData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Handles pending character selection UI updates and text validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if character selection is pending (g_nPendingCharacterSelection == -1)\n2. If pending, verify control parameter contains valid data at offset 0xC\n3. Clear existing text in control handler slots 0x54 and 0x55\n4. Validate and add string ID 0xFA8 to control handler 0x54\n5. Validate and add string ID 0x140C to control handler 0x55\n6. Set UI text box state to pending (value 3)\n7. Return success code 1\n\nParameters:\n  pControlData (int): Pointer to control structure; offset +0xC contains validation flag\n\nReturns:\n  dword: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_nPendingCharacterSelection != -1, function skips all processing and returns immediately\n  - If g_bUITextBoxPending is already 3, clears text handlers without re-adding strings\n  - String IDs (0xFA8, 0x140C) are validated before text box insertion\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n  g_nPendingCharacterSelection: Character selection state flag (-1 = pending)\n  g_aPendingControlHandlers[]: Array of UI control handler pointers\n  g_bUITextBoxPending: UI text box pending state (3 = active/pending)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x54: Index into control handler array for primary text box\n  0x55: Index into control handler array for secondary text box\n  0xFA8: String ID for primary text content\n  0x140C: String ID for secondary text content\n  3: Pending state value for g_bUITextBoxPending\n  0xC: Offset in pControlData for validation flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:5c22dede0f74ae8b02dbfc7aae0ebe58",
