      "name": "GetShardTableEntry",
      "signature": "uint GetShardTableEntry(int nShardIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Retrieves a validated entry from the shard table and returns a field offset.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the shard table base address from global DAT_6fa97c98\n2. Index into table using nShardIndex * 4 (DWORD array)\n3. Validate that retrieved pointer is non-NULL\n4. If NULL, invoke FogAssert and call FatalErrorExit (crash)\n5. Return the DWORD value at offset +0x1c from the retrieved pointer\n\nParameters:\n- nShardIndex (ECX, int): Zero-based index into shard table\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Value at offset 0x1c from indexed shard structure\n  \nError Handling:\n- NULL pointer in table triggers assertion and fatal exit\n- No return on error path (process terminates)\n\nField Structure:\nThe returned offset suggests accessing a field in a shard descriptor structure:\n  Offset 0x1c: DWORD value (possibly handle, ID, or pointer to nested data)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1c (28): Fixed offset into shard structure\n- 4: DWORD element size in table array\n\nNotes:\n- __fastcall convention: parameter in ECX register\n- Table lookup validates shard index is valid/initialized\n- Field at +0x1c appears to be a critical resource identifier",
