      "name": "ReleaseControlUIResources",
      "signature": "void ReleaseControlUIResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Algorithm:\n1. Release base UI control CEL file resources (15 fixed indices)\n2. Check if Expansion MPQ is available\n3. If Expansion MPQ exists, release 4 additional Expansion control resources\n4. Release common control resources (15 more indices)\n5. Check if primary control handler [0xa7] is allocated\n6. If allocated, release primary handler and dependent resources:\n   - Release handler [0xa7] and set to null\n   - Release handlers [0xa8], [0xaf], [0xcb], [0xcc]\n   - Release 5 loops of array-based control handlers\n   - Release 2 special control CEL files (DAT_6fa97bc4, DAT_6fa97bd8)\n7. Check Expansion MPQ again for secondary Expansion controls\n8. If Expansion MPQ exists, release additional Expansion handler loops (2 loops)\n9. Release final standard control resources (6 indices)\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: None (void - cleanup function)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Expansion controls only released if Expansion MPQ is present\n- Secondary Expansion controls depend on primary handler allocation\n- Multiple array-based control handler loops use ESI for pointer iteration\n- Handler [0xa7] acts as a master flag for Expansion control allocation\n\nLoop Details:\nLoop 1 (0x6fa97b1c-0x6fa97b30): 5 elements, stride 4 bytes\nLoop 2 (0x6fa97b30-0x6fa97b44): 5 elements, stride 4 bytes\nLoop 3 (0x6fa97b44-0x6fa97b58): 5 elements, stride 4 bytes\nLoop 4 (0x6fa97b58-0x6fa97b6c): 5 elements, stride 4 bytes\nLoop 5 (0x6fa97b6c-0x6fa97b80): 5 elements, stride 4 bytes\nLoop 6 (0x6fa97bb0-0x6fa97bbc): 3 elements, stride 4 bytes\nLoop 7 (0x6fa97b9c-0x6fa97ba8): 3 elements, stride 4 bytes\nLoop 8 (0x6fa97af4-0x6fa97b08): 5 elements, stride 4 bytes\nLoop 9 (0x6fa97b08-0x6fa97b1c): 5 elements, stride 4 bytes\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xa7: Primary Expansion handler index\n0xa40: Offset to handler allocation flag in g_aPendingControlHandlers array\n0x6fa97a14-0x6fa97af0: Control handler array indices (base and standard UI)\n0x6fa97b1c-0x6fa97bbc: Loop boundary addresses for array-based handlers\n\nError Handling: None - unconditional resource release\n\nResource Types: All calls target ReleaseCelFile() for CEL (sprite/image) resource cleanup",
