      "name": "ProcessIntroVideoInitialization",
      "signature": "void ProcessIntroVideoInitialization(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes and displays the intro video after processing pending Windows messages.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Process all pending Windows messages (PeekMessageA loop):\n   - Filter out mouse movement, key input, and system messages\n   - Dispatch remaining messages for normal window handling\n   - Continue until message queue is empty\n2. Check CPU for SSE2 support (CheckCpuLacksFeatures):\n   - If supported: use 640x292 resolution string\n   - If not supported: use resolution flag 2 (alternative resolution)\n3. Prepare video path:\n   - Copy resolution string to local buffer using optimized dword/byte copy\n   - Get locale identifier from GetLocaleString\n   - Format file path: \"video\\%s\\d2intro%s.bik\" (resolution-specific intro)\n4. Open intro video file (SFileOpenFileEx):\n   - If file not found (ENOFILE): try alternative path \"d2intro.bik\"\n   - If file opened: close the handle (will be reopened by video engine)\n5. Display intro video (GfxDispatchMethod38):\n   - Pass resolution flag to control animation timing\n6. Configure Battle.net auxiliary settings:\n   - Read Battle.net Aux setting from registry\n   - If setting exists: format with locale ID separator\n   - Write formatted setting back to registry\n\nParameters: void\n\nReturns: void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- CPU SSE2 support check affects intro animation speed (resolution determines frame rate)\n- Video file path is locale-specific (%s substitutions for resolution and locale)\n- Missing intro video files silently use fallback path without warning\n- Registry values may be empty; empty result is not treated as error\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x1: PM_REMOVE flag for PeekMessageA (remove processed messages)\n- 0x202-0x208: Windows message codes for mouse/keyboard input (WM_RBUTTONDOWN, etc.)\n- 0x12, 0x102: System messages (WM_QUIT, WM_CHAR) to skip dispatch\n- Resolution flag 2: Non-SSE2 alternative resolution setting\n\nStructure Layout - tagMSG (at ESP+0x20, 20 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type      Description\n  0x00    0x04  hwnd            void*     Window handle\n  0x04    0x04  message         uint      Message ID\n  0x08    0x04  wParam          uint      First parameter\n  0x0c    0x04  lParam          int       Second parameter\n  0x10    0x04  time            uint      Message time\n  0x14    0x04  pt              Point     Cursor position",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:f386ebd120fc57a956a497ee9fc59c17",
