      "name": "InitializeGameUIStateAndRecreateUI",
      "signature": "dword InitializeGameUIStateAndRecreateUI(void)",
      "calling_convention": "unknown",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Initialize game UI state and trigger recreation of all UI objects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x59] = 2 to flag pending control handler state\n2. Call InitializeGameUIAndRecreateObjects() to fully reinitialize UI system\n3. Return success code 1 to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - function takes no parameters (void __stdcall)\n\nReturns:\ndword - Always returns 1 indicating successful initialization trigger\n\nDescription:\nServes as entry point for UI system reinitialization. Typically called during state\ntransitions such as disconnection, realm changes, or character load events. This\nfunction sets a control handler status flag (indicating UI rebuild is pending) and\nthen delegates to InitializeGameUIAndRecreateObjects() which performs the actual\nUI recreation including palette initialization, object creation, and state cleanup.\n\nRelated Functions:\nInitializeGameUIAndRecreateObjects - Performs the actual UI system recreation\nDispatchInventoryItemHandler - Called to clean up existing UI objects\nSetGlobalConfig - Resets global configuration state\nCreateObjectByTypeFactory - Creates individual UI objects",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
