      "name": "RequestGameShutdown",
      "signature": "int RequestGameShutdown(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Requests graceful game shutdown by stopping the message loop.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call StopMessageLoop() to halt message processing\n2. Return success indicator (1 = true)\n\nParameters:\n  (none)\n\nReturns:\n  1 (int) - Shutdown request acknowledged (true/success)\n\nPurpose:\n  Wrapper function for initiating application exit. Used as callback/event handler\n  referenced from UI controls and game state management code.\n\nImplementation Notes:\n  - Simple wrapper for StopMessageLoop() with immediate return\n  - Return value indicates successful shutdown initiation\n  - Called from multiple initialization/control contexts via function pointer storage",
