      "comment": "Initialize Bnet login screen UI objects and message pump.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if Ordinal_10002 returns non-zero (skip init if true)\n2. Call FUN_6fa83a50 to validate param_2 data\n3. If validation fails (returns < 0 or >= 3), reset RNG and return early\n4. Process pending control handlers array (dispatch up to g_dwGameObjectCount handlers)\n5. Reset object count and set Bnet connection state flags\n6. Conditional branch on g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x5a]:\n   - If null: Create ConfigTypeA + BnetLoginUnitTypeA objects\n   - If non-null: Create ConfigTypeB + BnetLoginUnitTypeB objects\n7. Create appropriate sub-config object based on branch\n8. Set unit flags (value 1) on all created objects\n9. Validate string ID 0x147b and add text to UI\n10. Install Bnet disconnect handler\n11. Call Ordinal_10021 (unknown operation)\n12. Enter message pump with HandleBnetConnectionStateChange handler\n13. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\n  nParam1: Unknown parameter (ECX) - used in Ordinal_10002 path\n  pbData: Validation data pointer (EDX) - validated via FUN_6fa83a50\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Validation failed or early exit condition met\n  1 - Successfully initialized and entered message pump loop\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  g_dwGameObjectCount, _g_dwBnetConnectionActive, g_dwBnetLoginState\n  g_aPendingControlHandlers[], _g_pBnetDisconnectHandler",
