      "name": "ProcessCharacterCreation",
      "signature": "void ProcessCharacterCreation(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes character creation flow including validation, UI initialization, and state transitions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check character count via FUN_6fa83a50 - if valid (1-2), initialize character select screen\n2. Check Ordinal_10046 (net ready state) and Ordinal_10002 (auth state)\n3. If auth successful: log authorization, send create character command via Ordinal_10008\n4. Initialize inventory dispatch loop for pending controls (g_dwGameObjectCount entries)\n5. Set BnetConnectionActive=1, LoginState=0\n6. Branch based on character slot availability (g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x5a]):\n   - Slot available: Create controls 0xd7/0xd8/0xd9 (standard slots)\n   - Slot unavailable: Create controls 0xf0/0xf3/0xf2 (alternate slots)\n7. Set control flags, add text, register disconnect handler\n8. Enter message pump loop for BnetShutdown processing\n9. Post-pump: Check BnetLoginState for user cancellation\n   - If cancelled: Dispatch cleanup and return\n   - If success (LoginState==0): Process Ordinal_10046 result\n10. Result switch on Ordinal_10046 return value:\n    - 0x00: Success - log creation, call FUN_6fa84b60(1), copy character hash, set flags\n    - 0x14: Character exists - show exists dialog, call InitializeControlsPanel\n    - 0x02: Show error 0x145b - generic error dialog\n    - 0x0a-0x0c, default: Show error 0x145c/0x145d with appropriate dialog\n11. All paths dispatch pending inventory and reset g_dwGameObjectCount\n12. Handlers: Ordinal_10046 (net status), Ordinal_10002 (auth check), Ordinal_10008 (send create command)\n\nParameters:\n  None (void)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, processes state changes and UI updates\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Character count check (1-2 valid) causes early exit to InitializeCharacterSelectScreen\n  - Auth failure or cancel triggers StopMessageLoop early exit path\n  - All error codes (0x02, 0x0a-0x0c, others) show localized error dialogs\n  - Stack frame 0x718 bytes accommodates multiple Unicode string buffers\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x6fa938cc = \"Authorized by Shard\" message\n  0x6fa938ac = \"Send Create Character to Shard\" message\n  0x6fa9387c = \"Error from MCP trying to create\" message (0x14 case)\n  0x6fa93854 = \"Character already exists\" message (0x14 case)\n  0x6fa9383c = \"Created Character\" message (success case)\n  0x145b = Error string ID 2\n  0x145c = Error string ID default\n  0x145d = Error string ID 0xa-0xc\n  0x147b = Character creation success dialog text\n  g_aPendingControlHandlers = Global array of UI control pointers\n  g_dwGameObjectCount = Count of pending controls (0-0x40 valid)\n  g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x53] = Character data pointer\n  g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x5a] = Slot availability flag (0=available)\n  0x3f (63) = MAX_CHILDREN limit for g_dwGameObjectCount\n  0xd7/0xd8/0xd9 = Standard character slot UI control IDs\n  0xf0/0xf2/0xf3 = Alternate character slot UI control IDs\n  g_dwBnetConnectionActive offset 0x68 = Connection active flag\n  g_dwBnetLoginState offset 0x88 = Login state counter (0=idle, >0=active)\n  g_pBnetDisconnectHandler offset 0xa0 = Disconnect callback pointer\n  Character hash table size 0x7fffffff = Maximum copy size (copies entire table)\n\nError Handling:\n  - Ordinal_10046 < 0: Check not performed (assumes not ready)\n  - Auth failure (Ordinal_10002==0): Logs failure, calls StopMessageLoop and returns\n  - MessagePumpLoop cancellation (g_dwBnetLoginState!=0): Cleans up and returns early\n  - Array overflow (g_dwGameObjectCount >= 0x40): Triggers FogAssert and FatalErrorExit\n  - Character exists (0x14): Shows localized error dialog via ValidateStringId/sprintf\n\nStructure Layout (g_aPendingControlHandlers array elements):\n  Offset | Size | Field                              | Type     | Description\n  0x00   | 4    | Control Pointer                    | void*    | UI control/object pointer\n  0x53*4 | var  | Character Data                     | struct   | Character info at index 0x53\n  0x58*4 | 4    | Game State Value                   | uint     | At index 0x58: state=3 after creation\n  0x5a*4 | 4    | Slot Availability                  | uint     | At index 0x5a: 0=available, else unavailable",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
