      "name": "ResetGameUIAndObjectState",
      "signature": "void ResetGameUIAndObjectState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Resets game UI and game object state, reinitializing core game structures.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dispatch handlers for all active UI objects using g_dwUIObjectCount\n2. Dispatch handlers for all pending control handlers using g_dwGameObjectCount\n3. Reset UI object count and control handler counters to 0\n4. Call SetGlobalConfig(0) to reset configuration state\n5. If g_bPaletteReinitFlag set: Compare palette paths and call InitActPalette\n6. Release all game units via ReleaseAllUnits()\n7. Clear hash table and perform cleanup via ClearHashTableAndCleanup()\n8. Set stored value to 1 via SetStoredValue(1)\n9. Create and initialize 3 new UI objects (descriptors 3 and 4, plus DAT_6fa8f830)\n10. Handle palette reinitialization for sky palette with path comparison logic\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global game state\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Palette reinitialization involves two separate path comparison sequences\n- String comparison is done byte-by-byte for up to 260-character paths\n- MAX_CHILDREN assertion checked before each UI object creation (limit 0x3f)\n- Palette reinit flag toggled during initialization sequence\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x5a: Pending control handler array offset where palette reinit flag stored\n0x3f: Maximum children allowed in UI object array (63 objects)\n0x60d: Assertion line number in source file\n0xffffffff: FatalErrorExit parameter (force exit)\n256, 4, 260: Local string buffer sizes for path manipulation\n\nError Handling:\n- FogAssert called if UI object count exceeds 0x3f, triggers FatalErrorExit\n- Invalid palette paths bypass InitActPalette but log assertion\n- String comparison loops detect null terminators to safely handle varying path lengths",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:546c17e22a38a8e15c8829671ea3e893",
