      "name": "LoadCharacterSelectResources",
      "signature": "void LoadCharacterSelectResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Loads character selection UI resources from data files.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if resources already loaded via guard (g_aPendingControlHandlers[0xa7] != 0)\n2. If guard set, skip entire initialization (resources are cached); return\n3. Load UI button graphics: MediumSelButtonBlank using wsprintfA to format path\n4. Call LoadCelImage to load CEL image file into control handler array index 0xaf\n5. Check expansion pack availability via CheckExpansionMpqExists()\n6. Conditionally load expansion-specific images (Assassin, Druid) based on expansion availability\n7. Load base character class images (Amazon, Necromancer, Barbarian, Sorceress, Paladin)\n8. Conditionally load expansion-only shadow variants if expansion pack present\n9. Store all image handles in g_aPendingControlHandlers array with character class indices\n10. Return to caller (initialization complete; function is idempotent via guard)\n\nParameters:\nNone - reads global guard g_aPendingControlHandlers[0xa7]\n\nReturns:\nvoid (side effect: populates global control handler array with CEL image handles)\n\nError Handling:\nNone - LoadCelImage failures are silent; NULL pointers may be stored\n\nSpecial Cases:\nExpansion pack conditional: CheckExpansionMpqExists() determines image set loaded\nGuard check prevents redundant loading on subsequent calls",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:d0a5c22af621ee582beefa5bad6bb5ea",
