      "name": "InitializeLocaleSpecificData",
      "signature": "void InitializeLocaleSpecificData(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes locale-specific configuration data for Japanese language.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetLanguageLocaleId() to retrieve current system locale identifier\n2. Compare returned locale ID with 0x9 (Japanese locale code)\n3. If locale is NOT 9, skip all initializations and return\n4. If locale IS 9, initialize 10 global data values with locale-specific offsets\n5. Return from function\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function called with no parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Modifies 10 global data locations as side effect.\n\nBehavior:\nThis function is a locale-specific initializer that sets up configuration data when the system\nlocale is set to Japanese (locale ID 9). Each MOV instruction initializes a global dword with\na specific hexadecimal value, likely representing offsets or indices into locale-specific tables.\n\nGlobal Locations Modified (10 total):\n0x6fa905b8 = 0x9b    (155)\n0x6fa8fb98 = 0x14e   (334)\n0x6fa8fbc8 = 0x184   (388)\n0x6fa8fbf8 = 0x1ba   (442)\n0x6fa8fc88 = 0xf0    (240)\n0x6fa8fcb8 = 0x146   (326)\n0x6fa90858 = 0x9c    (156)\n0x6fa91b18 = 0x20e   (526)\n0x6fa91b48 = 0x23f   (575)\n0x6fa925f8 = 0x46    (70)\n0x6fa927a8 = 0xee    (238)\n\nCallers: FUN_6fa85070 (likely main initialization routine)\n\nNotes:\n- Function uses conditional branching: if locale != 9, all MOV operations are skipped via JNZ\n- All writes are unconditional dwords (4 bytes each)\n- No error handling or validation of locale ID\n- Values appear to be indices or offsets (small hex values in range 0x46-0x23f)",
