      "name": "QuickSortIterative",
      "signature": "void QuickSortIterative(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Iterative quicksort implementation with explicit stack.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if count < 2 or element size is 0\n2. Use explicit stacks (apLoStack, apHiStack) to avoid recursion\n3. For partitions <= 8 elements, use selection sort\n4. For larger partitions:\n   a. Select median pivot via middle element\n   b. Partition array around pivot using comparison callback\n   c. Push larger subpartition to stack, process smaller one\n5. Pop and process remaining partitions until stack empty\n\nParameters:\n- pBase (void*): Base pointer to array\n- nCount (int): Number of elements\n- nElemSize (int): Size of each element in bytes\n- pfnCompare (void*): Comparison callback (a,b) returns <0, 0, >0\n\nReturns:\n- void (sorts array in-place)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 8: Insertion sort threshold for small partitions\n- 30: Maximum stack depth (handles 2^30 elements)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:b83338c5610ff816794a2473b0b3c2c5",
