      "name": "ReadStreamLocked",
      "signature": "uint ReadStreamLocked(void * pvBuffer, uint dwElementSize, uint dwElementCount, void * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Reads data from a stream with thread-safety via critical section locking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire stream lock via EnterCriticalSection\n2. Call internal read function to read elements into buffer\n3. Release stream lock via LeaveCriticalSection\n4. Return count of elements read\n\nParameters:\n- pvBuffer (void*): Destination buffer for read data\n- dwElementSize (uint): Size of each element in bytes\n- dwElementCount (uint): Number of elements to read\n- pStream (void*): Stream handle containing critical section at offset 0x20\n\nReturns:\n- Number of elements successfully read (may be less than requested on EOF/error)",
