      "name": "DisplayRuntimeError",
      "signature": "void DisplayRuntimeError(void * pErrorCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Reports a runtime error by displaying a formatted message to the console or GUI.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search error code table (g_pErrorCodeTable) to find matching entry\n2. Check global flags (g_dwErrorOutputMode, g_dwConsoleOutputFlag) to determine output mode\n3. If flag indicates console output: write error message directly to stdout\n4. Otherwise: build detailed error message including program path, error description, and error code\n5. If module path exceeds 60 chars, truncate with \"...\"\n6. Display error dialog via Visual C++ runtime (FUN_6fa8b6f8)\n\nParameters:\n  pErrorCode (void*): Pointer to error code in error lookup table\n\nReturns:\n  void - Does not return if error dialog is displayed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  DAT_6fa97d98=1 or (DAT_6fa97d98=0 AND DAT_6fa97d9c=1): Console output mode\n  pErrorCode=0xFC: Skip output and return immediately\n  pErrorCode=0x0: Use default \"Program: \" with \"Runtime Error!\" prefix\n  GetModuleFileNameA may fail (returns 0); falls back to \"<program name unknown>\"\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x104 (260): MAX_PATH buffer size for module filename\n  0x3c (60): Maximum displayed path length before truncation\n  0x8, 0x2: Error table entry stride and bounds\n  0xFC: Special error code for silent return\n  0xfffffff4: STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE constant for GetStdHandle",
