      "name": "InitializeCodePageLocale",
      "signature": "int InitializeCodePageLocale(int nCodePage)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes character type lookup tables for a specific code page.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter critical section 0x19 to synchronize access to global tables\n2. Retrieve the Windows code page ID via FUN_6fa8b10d(nCodePage)\n3. If code page matches cached DAT_6fa980b0, skip re-initialization (already loaded)\n4. If code page is 0 or invalid, handle error path\n5. For known code pages (0-6 predefined ranges), clear g_abCharacterTypeTable and load from preset range tables:\n   - Each range has start/end byte pairs that define character ranges\n   - Each byte range gets marked with flag bits (0x4 for lead bytes, 0x8 for trail bytes)\n6. For unknown code pages, call GetCPInfo API to retrieve lead byte ranges dynamically:\n   - Clear character type table\n   - Parse LeadByte pairs from CPINFO structure\n   - Mark all lead bytes with 0x4 flag, trail bytes with 0x8 flag\n   - Iterate 0x01-0xFF setting appropriate type flags\n7. Call FUN_6fa8b157(nCodePage) to generate multi-byte handling table\n8. Exit critical section\n9. Return 0 on success, -1 on failure\n\nParameters:\n   nCodePage (int): Windows code page identifier (932=Shift-JIS, 936=GBK, 949=Korean, etc.)\n\nReturns:\n   (int): 0 on success, -1 if code page not supported or initialization failed\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n   g_abCharacterTypeTable: 257-byte character classification array (index 0 unused)\n   DAT_6fa980b0: Current code page cache\n   DAT_6fa980cc: Multi-byte character support flag (0=single-byte, 1=multi-byte)\n   DAT_6fa982e4: Multi-byte table pointer\n   DAT_6fa980c0/c4/c8: Code page-specific parameters\n\nCritical Sections:\n   Protects against concurrent code page changes during table initialization\n\nDependencies:\n   FUN_6fa8b10d: GetCPInfo wrapper or predefined code page lookup\n   FUN_6fa8b157: Build multi-byte table from CPINFO\n   FUN_6fa8b1b3: Post-initialization handler\n   FUN_6fa8b18a: Error handler\n   GetCPInfo (Windows API): Retrieve code page info for dynamic initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n   - Code page 0: Error path (DAT_6fa97f1c check required)\n   - Cached code pages (0-5): Use preset tables instead of API\n   - Unknown code pages: Fall back to GetCPInfo API\n   - Single-byte vs multi-byte: Flag determines trail byte handling rules",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
