      "name": "SetStreamPropertyFlag",
      "signature": "int SetStreamPropertyFlag(uint dwPropertyIndex, int nFlagMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Clear or set the 0x80 flag bit in a stream property table entry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current property flags from g_pStreamPropertyTables[dwPropertyIndex >> 5] + offset\n2. If nFlagMode == 0x8000: Clear bit 0x80 (AND flags with 0x7F)\n3. Else if nFlagMode == 0x4000: Set bit 0x80 (OR flags with 0x80)\n4. Else: Call GetTlsContextSlotPointer(), set error code to 0x16, return -1\n5. Write modified flags back to stream property entry\n6. Calculate return value based on original flag state using NEG/SBB trick\n7. Return (originalFlagWas0x80 ? 0xffffc000 : 0) + 0x8000\n\nParameters:\n  dwPropertyIndex (uint) - Index into stream property tables, used to select entry\n  nFlagMode (int) - Operation mode: 0x8000 to clear, 0x4000 to set, else error\n\nReturns:\n  int - Result code indicating prior flag state: 0x8000 if bit was clear, 0xffffc000 + 0x8000 if set\n  -1 - Error when nFlagMode is invalid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Invalid nFlagMode triggers error through TLS context (0x16 = error code)\n  Function returns -1 on error; success return value has semantic meaning\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x8000 - FLAG_CLEAR mode selector\n  0x4000 - FLAG_SET mode selector\n  0x80 - Active bit mask in property byte (bit 7)\n  0x7F - Mask to clear bit 7 (0x80)\n  0x1F - Mask for bit shift (32-entry block select)\n  0x5 - Right shift count to select 32-entry block\n  0x24 - Entry stride in property tables (36 bytes per entry)",
